11:17:22 PM | E2E Test Suite: Marketplace Item & Listing Management Lifecycle > 2. My Items Management (GET /api/v1/items/my-items) > 2.1 Chauffeur retrieves and filters My Items dashboard feed (default, price range, and keyword search) (GET /api/v1/items/my-items) | stdout

📝 USER STORY:
As a Selling Chauffeur
I want to view, filter by price range, and search my listed items
So that I can effectively manage my active inventory on the marketplace

📋 BUSINESS RULES & QUERY PAYLOAD SPECIFICATIONS:
• Endpoint: GET /api/v1/items/my-items
• Authentication: Bearer JWT Token required (extracts seller userId)
• Query Parameters Handled:
  - minPrice (number): Filters items with price >= minPrice ($gte query)
  - maxPrice (number): Filters items with price <= maxPrice ($lte query)
  - searchTerm (string): Case-insensitive keyword matching on title ($regex, $options: 'i')
  - condition (string): Optional filter by condition ('New' | 'Used' | 'Refurbished')
  - limit (number): Page size limit (default: 10, max: 50)
  - cursor (string): Base64URL-encoded pagination pointer ({ _id }) for infinite scroll
• Default Sorting: Newest listings first (_id: -1)

